00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.640
Today's lesson is going to be a fun one.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.360
Поехали.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.180
Today we step into a cozy Russian kitchen.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.780
Our word of the day is хлеб.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.780
The Russian word is хлеб.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.000
хлеб- хлеб.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.820
It sounds a little like love if you stretch your imagination.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.720
The Russians often say хлеб when they mean the stuff of life.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.020
Repeat after me.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:29.880
хлеб.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.440
Here is a simple sentence.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:32.780
Я ем хлеб.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.020
Я ем хлеб.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:34.700
А я ем хлеб.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:34.940
А я ем хлеб.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.440
Now we build more kitchen words that go with хлеб.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.580
The next word is молоко.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:41.480
молоко.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:42.160
молоко.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.320
It starts with mala like malt.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.400
Think of milky malt drinks.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:47.940
Я пью молоко.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.120
Я пью молоко.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:49.740
Я пью молоко.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:50.080
Я drink milk.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.000
Next comes яблока.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.300
Яблока яблока.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.600
Яблока almost sounds like ямиблока, a crunchy block of fruit.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.140
Это красная яблока, это красная яблока.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:02.420
This is a red apple.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:06.460
Here is sour, sour, say sour like sour.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.440
Imagine a fancy sour offering you cheese.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.960
Сыр вкусный, сыр вкусный.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.120
The cheese is delicious.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.080
Now we add мясо.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:15.680
Мясо.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:16.760
Моясо.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.300
Моясо has my, my favorite meat.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.880
Мясо на тарелке.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.120
Моясо на тарелке.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.280
Meat is on the plate.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.520
Next are ovащи, ovащи, ovащи.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.280
Ovo like oval.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.480
Манивощи болтев are oval shaped.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.060
Ovoщи полезные.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.360
Ovoщи полезные.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:35.020
Ващи болтев are healthy.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.560
Our next word is soup, soup, soup.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.380
It is basically the same word as English soup, an easy win.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.500
Горячий суп, горячий суп, hot soup.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.760
Here is tea, tea, tea.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.060
It sounds like tea.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.720
Доспайся чай тию у родину.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.180
Чай с сахаром, чай с сахаром, ти вытшугар.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:56.780
Next comes coffee.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:57.820
Coffee, coffee.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.240
Coffee sounds like coffee.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:00.400
Полмостой дентяков.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.500
Coffee горячий.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.440
Coffee горячий.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.440
The coffee is hot.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:05.760
Now we learn a describing word.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:06.480
Вкусный.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:07.200
Вкусный.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.740
Вкус sounds like taste.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.620
Your taste but say вкусный.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.160
Этот хлеб вкусный.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.500
Этот хлеб вкусный.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:14.700
This bread is delicious.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.360
Remember home from a few lessons ago?

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:18.020
Дом.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:18.540
Дом.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:18.980
Дом.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:19.720
That means house.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.500
Now picture a kitchen inside that house.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:23.900
Where we eat our food.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:26.160
Our last kitchen word is еду.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:26.760
Еду.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:27.440
Еду.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:27.960
Еду.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.040
Я люблю еду.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:29.700
Я люблю еду.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:30.740
Я люблю еду.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:31.260
I love food.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.680
In Russian every now belong to a team.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.000
The teams are called masculine, feminine or neuter.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.980
These teams change how we say describing words.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:41.320
хлеб is masculine.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.900
This is why we say вкусный хлеб.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:45.260
Яблоко is neuter.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.500
This is why we say вкусное яблоко.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:50.240
English does not change adjectives for teams.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:53.300
But Russian gives every now and its own team color.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.200
In Russia bread is treated with great respect.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:59.180
It is often placed in the center of the table.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.580
People say хлеб всему голова.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.200
хлеб всему голова.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.160
Bread is the head of everything.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.840
Guests are welcomed with bread and salt.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:09.820
That shows world and hospitality.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.680
Do you remember what хлеб means?

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:13.960
Say it out loud.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:14.600
хлеб.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:14.980
Bread.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:19.820
For kids, draw your favorite meal and label three items using today's words.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.940
For adults, next time you make breakfast, say the rice mimimi is out loud for everything on your plate.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.760
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.160
Want to know secret about чай?

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.660
Did you know that the Russian word чай

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:38.620
and the English word t are actually cousins from the same ancient route?

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:41.600
This word started in China as чай.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:45.620
It traveled along the Silk Road through Persian and Turkish traders.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:52.140
It finally arrived in Russian in the 17th century when tea became popular at the royal court.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:57.900
Be careful though, the Russian word magazine sounds like magazine, but actually means shop.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.680
Next time you see pack-up of tea, remember it's cousin чай.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.280
They both come from the same Chinese route.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:08.180
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:08.900
Молодец.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:10.300
That means well done.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:15.220
Remember every expert started as a beginner practicing today's words out loud,

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.320
even just once and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:19.660
See you next time.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:20.120
Пока.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:21.600
That's Russian for buy.

